+++++ b/.garura/product/product-os/features/fn-730/feature.md
++@@ -1,10 +1,10 @@
++-# Feature: Update, edit or delete a plan file, and connect it to its issues
+++# Feature: The /update-plan session — instructions, checks, one approval, one landing on the plan's branch
++ 
++ ## What it does
++-add, move, drop or finish a node, or delete a plan — in the plan file and in the tracker (create, re-parent, close) together. Work can go on in the plan file; the sync brings the tracker up to date.
+++a person opens a session on one plan with `/update-plan <id>` or a description, gives instructions in their own words, and approves; the play lands the changes in the plan file and GitHub together, on the plan's own branch. Changing an epic's or a story's text is one more instruction (#909 folded in).
++ 
++ ## Agent intent (ICE)
++-- Goal: Any change to a plan reaches both the plan file and the tracker.
++-- Limit: Never touches branches or code.
++-- Fails if: the tracker is left behind, or a dropped node stays open.
++-- Checked by: a test edits a plan three ways and the compare finds no difference.
+++- Goal: Every instruction the person approved reaches the plan file and GitHub, in one landing on the plan's branch, and they agree afterwards.
+++- Limit: Nothing is written before a plain "approved", except the one step that gives a plan with no branch its branch (main's plan file set first, then the cut). It never merges a branch and never changes code.
+++- Fails if: a write happens before approval, other than that branch step; GitHub is left behind or ahead of the plan file; a dropped item stays open; anything changes that the person did not approve; it switches away from a branch with uncommitted work.
+++- Checked by: a test session with several instructions (add, move, drop, finish, change a story's text, set Status and Direction), approved once; the compare of the plan file with GitHub finds no difference, and nothing outside the list changed.
++diff --git a/.garura/project/issues/720/specs/design.md b/.garura/project/issues/720/specs/design.md
++index 9eb375a2c..4c5c202b8 100644
++--- a/.garura/project/issues/720/specs/design.md
+++++ b/.garura/project/issues/720/specs/design.md
++@@ -57,6 +57,11 @@ Small changes get one line. Big ones are shown and confirmed before they join th
++ epic, moving a feature between slices, a model change, closing an item with open work under it.
++ Nothing is written to GitHub, the model or the plan file during the session.
++ 
+++**The one write before approval.** When the plan has no branch, getting onto it (above) sets main's
+++plan file to In Progress with the branch named, commits that on main, and cuts the branch. That is
+++bookkeeping that makes the plan's branch exist, not a change the person approves; it is the only
+++write before "approved". (Found by the review of PR #995, finding F1, 2026-10-30.)
+++
++ ## How it ends: approve or reject
++ 
++ - The play shows the whole list and asks: approved or rejected.
++@@ -80,7 +85,8 @@ propose-change, check-change and merge-change, like all its other work.
++ 
++ - A person sets every Status and Direction; nothing is worked out, and there are no roll-ups (an
++   epic can be closed with open stories).
++-- It never cuts a branch except as above, never merges one, and never touches code.
+++- Nothing is written before a plain "approved", except the branch step above for a plan with no
+++  branch. It never cuts a branch except as above, never merges one, and never touches code.
++ - Changes go through sub-agents and skills; no hand edits of the model or the issues.
++ - It writes down which item kinds a plan may hold (#917, point 3).
